# Architecture (air-finance-app)

## Monorepo

- `apps/web`: main Vite SPA; primary source for `pages/`, `components/`, `hooks/`, `services/`, `stores/`, `routes/`
- `apps/mobile-webview`: WebView shell and native-adjacent config
- `packages/shared`: cross-app types, utilities, and shared constants

## Routing

- Route definitions and lazy page imports live under `apps/web/src/routes/` (and related route config)
- Many top-level flows under `apps/web/src/pages/` mirroring product areas (dashboard, transactions, accounts, open finance, admin, SEO, etc.)

## API layer

- Central Axios instance: `apps/web/src/services/apiClient.ts` (or current equivalent path)
- Feature services under `apps/web/src/services/` encapsulate HTTP and DTO mapping

## State

- Zustand stores include auth, company, preferences, sidebar, statement, transaction, maintenance, theme, notifications (names may vary slightly; search `stores/`)

## Layouts

- `LayoutDefault`, `LayoutAuth`, `ViewDefault` under `layouts/` provide consistent chrome and page structure

## SEO

- `react-helmet-async` for metadata; dedicated SEO-oriented pages under `pages/seo/` where applicable

## New feature flow

1. Add or extend a route in `routes/`
2. Add page under `pages/<feature>/` (split `desktop.tsx` / `mobile.tsx` when the project pattern exists)
3. Add service methods in `services/`
4. Add TanStack Query hooks and/or Zustand actions in `hooks/` and `stores/`
5. Compose UI with existing design primitives under `components/`

## Scale

- The codebase is large (hundreds of components and hooks). Prefer extending existing modules over duplicating patterns.
